Stop [E3005]: #Pre contract failed: cents must be positive
  --> PreBreach.jet:9 in run
    |
9 |     print("second: {add_fee(0)}")
    |                     ^^^^^^^
 Why: A `#Pre` (argument claim, checked at entry) or `#Post` (`result` claim, checked before return) condition evaluated false at runtime. `#Pre contract failed: cents must be positive` is the clause's own message string. Checked in every build (not a debug/release split) — with file:line.
 Fix: Fix the caller (a failed `#Pre` means an argument violated the function's stated contract) or the function body (a failed `#Post` means it broke its own promise about the result).
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E3005
